Diagnostics that span more than one file. Each of these positions lives
in a file the user may never have opened, so the message has to name
the file as well as the line and column — the whole point of carrying
file identity in spans.

Two explicitly applied templates setting the same field is an error,
not a silent last-one-wins, and both sides of the collision are
located: the one being applied, and the one that already set it.

```console
$ hllc --build collision.hll
? 1
restart-unless-stopped.hll:2:11: field `restart.policy` set by both template `always_up` (at restart-always.hll:2:11) and template `mostly_up`—explicit templates must not conflict

```

A named volume must be declared before a service mounts it, and a
typo in the reference is reported against the reference's own position.

```console
$ hllc --build undeclared-volume.hll
? 1
undeclared-volume.hll:5:10: service `syncthing` references undeclared volume `snycthing-config`

```

The qualified form resolves against the aliased file's declarations, so
an alias that resolves to a real file with no such `volume` is a located
error rather than a silently invented volume.

```console
$ hllc --build unknown-qualified-volume.hll
? 1
unknown-qualified-volume.hll:5:10: no volume `medai` in `storage`

```

A codegen error raised inside an imported template reports the template's
file, not the entry file that applied it.

```console
$ hllc --build imported-codegen-error.hll
? 1
interpolating-template.hll:2:18: unknown interpolation `{{nmae}}`

```

`middleware` with no `router` has no Traefik router to attach itself
to. This used to build a service with the middleware silently missing;
it now fails, and the message carries the fix.

```console
$ hllc --build router-less-middleware.hll --out docker-compose.yml
? 1
router-less-middleware.hll:4:14: service `web` sets `middleware` but has no `router` to attach it to — add a router (`router { host: "web.example.com" }`) or drop the `middleware`

```
